**Theorem 4.4 (initialized source- and owner-preserving lift).** Let
$\widehat h$ be the resulting structural execution of any original
preparation/acquisition prefix or any $h\in\Omega$. Then

$$
\operatorname{end}(\widehat h)=\Gamma_+(Y(h)),\qquad
\operatorname{step}_{\Pi}(\Gamma_+(Y(h)),a)
 =\Gamma_+(Y(ha))
\tag{CSA.3}
$$

for each enabled lawful next native action $a$. The same local equation
represents its enabled raw-IN exit in $\partial_{\rm raw}\Omega$.
Disabled/unauthorized actions have the same nonexecution. Every actual
native cut has one structural cut, with the same output bits, raw fields,
source occurrence, tokens and receipt ordinal.

Proof. The foundation decodes to the actual native primitive entrance,
with no endowed source or future code bits. For every ordinary cell,
latch, Boolean, move, EX, TOK, seal/CTL and boundary-constructor row use
SSA Theorem 6.2's per-opcode proof, applied to these identical local roles.
The proof uses only the actual native finite pattern, so a bank, staged
descriptor or source cell has no different storage case. In particular
all emitted word-program instructions remain their full native expansions.

Existing finite fields use the same switch assignment proof. The additional
fresh-control case is Lemma 4.2. Mode/cursor tests and changes have their
actual finite encodings; raw and active tables remain distinct throughout
both bootstraps. Install is precisely RCA's bounded mode/PC change on
existing fields and one receipt, with its original Ready/owner guard.
There is no new ordinary-cell effect or early construction of $L,D_1$.
All effects are combined on actual overlapping roles before commitment.
This proves the local equation from any related pre-row record. Induction
from the foundation proves CSA.3 through boot, acquisition, both later
bootstraps and every subsequent row.

Raw IN changes the identical latch and PC and constructs the identical
receipt for either bit; the physical patch does not apply a canonical
input filter. Hence a noncanonical edge still has its raw structural
successor. The lawful domain does not include that successor. A failed
guard has no native effect and no patch. No later malformed semantics is
needed for either statement.

Each component's authority is the authority of its unique native field.
TOK changes the same finite permission fields; publication and availability
change at the same actual seal rows. Internal primitive probes do not become
actor-readable output. Thus source handlers still act on the same private
source; service replay still acts only on acquired banks. Fixed naming
preserves actual origins and copying chains. The inherited whole-source
service results therefore retain ordered grafts, genuine substitution,
whole-capacity guards, literal/numerical replies and executed rejects.
During a source WR the equation concerns raw bytes, without calling a
valid-tree decoder. Semantic annotations will be recovered from the same
history in §5. Under the stated atomic basis no additional maintenance
cuts occur, and no native installation/copy cut is removed. ∎

